[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 457,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 370,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62905,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 97,
        "headingId": 370,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Endometrioid stromal sarcoma is a low-grade malignant mesenchymal neoplasm resembling proliferative-type endometrial stroma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:17:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 458,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 371,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62906,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 97,
        "headingId": 371,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8931/3 Endometrioid stromal sarcoma, low grade</p>\r\n<p>8930/3 Endometrioid stromal sarcoma, high grade</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:17:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 459,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 372,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62907,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 97,
        "headingId": 372,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2C51.Y &amp; XH1S94 Other specified malignant neoplasms of peritoneum &amp; Endometrial stromal sarcoma, low grade</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:17:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 460,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 373,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62908,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 97,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:17:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62909,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 97,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:17:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62910,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 97,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours involve the abdomen/peritoneum, bowel wall, retroperitoneum, and other sites (in decreasing frequency) {24121169; 29293021}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:17:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62911,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 97,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There are usually signs and symptoms related to a pelvic/abdominal mass, followed by gastrointestinal and urinary symptoms, but the tumour may present as an incidental finding {24121169; 8253545}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:17:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62912,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 97,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Endometrioid stromal sarcoma of the peritoneum is rare.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:17:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62913,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 97,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:17:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62914,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 97,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours usually arise in association with endometriosis {24121169; 8968246; 10757398; 7293962}. Because molecular studies have not been performed on endometrioid stromal sarcomas of the peritoneum, it is unknown whether they have the same molecular alterations as their uterine counterparts.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:17:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62915,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 97,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours may involve one or multiple locations and range widely in size (up to 25&nbsp;cm), typically infiltrating underlying organs/tissues {8253545; 24121169}. They have a homogeneous solid and tan to yellow cut surface, but cystic degeneration may be seen, especially in cases associated with endometriosis {8253545}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:17:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62916,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 97,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours may lack the typical tongue pattern of invasion seen in their uterine counterparts, but they often display a multinodular growth. They are characterized by a diffuse growth of uniform small cells with scant cytoplasm, bland oval nuclei, and variable mitotic activity, resembling proliferative-type stroma. However, a fibromatous background (as reported in the ovary) can be seen. Other features include hyaline plaques, sex cord&ndash;like differentiation, endometrioid-type glands, smooth muscle differentiation, pseudopapillary growth, myxoid change, and prominence of foamy histiocytes. Vessels are typically arteriole-like and sometimes hyalinized, and tumour cells may be whorled around them {24121169; 8253545}. Transformation to a higher-grade sarcoma may occur {24121169}. Tumours are typically positive for CD10, ER, and PR; they may express smooth muscle markers (typically actin and desmin) and keratins, while areas of sex cord differentiation are often positive for inhibin and calretinin, among other sex cord markers {24121169}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:17:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62917,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 97,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:17:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62918,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 97,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:17:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62919,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 97,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> diffuse growth of small uniform cells with minimal cytological atypia, resembling proliferative-type endometrial stroma.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> presence of associated endometriosis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:17:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62920,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 97,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>This neoplasm is not usually staged.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:17:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62921,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 97,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours are associated with recurrences but have an indolent behaviour overall. In the largest series, more than half of the patients were alive without disease at the last follow-up. In that study, adverse prognostic factors included gastrointestinal involvement and association with a high-grade component {24121169}. Mitotic activity is not associated with prognosis {24121169; 8253545}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:17:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]